llvm-3.6.2 host patch 01: include/llvm/IR/ValueMap.h

ValueMap::hasMD() returns a std::unique_ptr as bool. unique_ptr's operator
bool is explicit, so `return MDMap;` is an ill-formed implicit conversion;
the gcc 4.8-era hosts 3.6.2 was released with accepted it, GCC 14 (and
recent libstdc++) rejects it ("cannot convert 'const std::unique_ptr<...>'
to 'bool' in return", 20 TUs under lib/CodeGen and lib/Transforms). Spell
the conversion out; same value, no effect on generated code.

diff --git a/include/llvm/IR/ValueMap.h b/include/llvm/IR/ValueMap.h
index f2ea405..f9a1a62 100644
--- a/include/llvm/IR/ValueMap.h
+++ b/include/llvm/IR/ValueMap.h
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ public:
 
   ~ValueMap() {}
 
-  bool hasMD() const { return MDMap; }
+  bool hasMD() const { return static_cast<bool>(MDMap); }
   MDMapT &MD() {
     if (!MDMap)
       MDMap.reset(new MDMapT);
